IMPORT prelude

-- California Revenue and Taxation Code, Division 2, Part 10 (Personal Income Tax) -- the 2025 tax of a full-year resident.
--
-- Edition: the Legislative Counsel's official bulk export (code tables updated 2026-10-03), deposited at
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ca-rtc-div2-part10-ch1-general-provisions-definitions-2026-10.txt (ss 17014, 17016)
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ca-rtc-div2-part10-ch2-imposition-of-tax-rates-credits-2026-10.txt (ss 17041-17054.1, 17053.5)
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ca-rtc-div2-part10-ch3-arts1-3-gross-income-inclusions-exclusions-2026-10.txt (s 17073.5)
-- and, for the figures the Franchise Tax Board recomputes each year (ss 17041(h), 17054(i), 17054.1(f), 17073.5(d)), the
-- FTB's 2025 publications deposited on 2026-10-24:
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ftb-2025-540-tax-rate-schedules.txt (transcribed in its .formulas.md)
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ftb-2025-540-booklet.txt
-- and recorded in ../../registers/annual-figures.json.
--
-- In: s 17014(a), (c), (d) and s 17016 (resident); s 17041(a), (b) with (h) and s 17045 (the 2025 rate schedules X, Y,
-- Z); s 17043 (1% on taxable income over $1,000,000); s 17054(a)-(f) with (i) (exemption credits: personal, senior,
-- blind, dependents, at the 2025 amounts); s 17054.1 (their phase-out); s 17053.5(a), (c) (renter's credit, 2025);
-- s 17073.5 (standard deduction, 2025 amounts).
--
-- Out: taxable years other than 2025 (`not covered`: the FTB figures for 2026 are not deposited); part-year residents and
-- nonresidents (`not covered`); California AGI itself (IRC s 62 via s 17072, with the Part 10 modifications: an input);
-- itemized deductions item by item (one total); the CalEITC (s 17052) and Young Child Tax Credit (s 17052.1), whose
-- amounts turn on an adjustment factor in the annual Budget Act and on form FTB 3514, not deposited; every other credit;
-- the alternative minimum tax; the FTB Tax Table for taxable income of $100,000 or less (the schedules are used instead:
-- NOTES.md finding 2); the standard deduction of a person who can be claimed as a dependent (IRC s 63(c)(5)).
--
-- Federal links (not imported): federal AGI and "dependent" (s 17056, IRC s 152) come from
-- subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986, as conformed by s 17024.5.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING, from the seat of the individual taxpayer. Expected values in the case file are hand-written. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT TAX ADVICE.

§ `Rev. & Tax. Code Part 10 -- the personal income tax of a California resident, 2025`

§§ `What this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `this encoding has the Franchise Tax Board's figures for the 2025 taxable year only`
    `the tax of a part-year resident or nonresident is not encoded`

DECLARE `Answer` IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `amount`  IS A NUMBER
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Filing status`

-- s 17042 (head of household), s 17045 (joint returns), s 17046 (surviving spouse); registered domestic partners are
-- treated as spouses (Family Code 297.5; the FTB forms say "Married/RDP"). Asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Filing status` IS ONE OF
    `single`
    `married or RDP filing jointly`
    `married or RDP filing separately`
    `head of household`
    `qualifying surviving spouse or RDP`

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a joint-type status` IF
        `status` EQUALS `married or RDP filing jointly`
    OR  `status` EQUALS `qualifying surviving spouse or RDP`

§§ `s 17014, s 17016 -- resident`

-- s 17014(a): "(1) Every individual who is in this state for other than a temporary or transitory purpose. (2) Every
-- individual domiciled in this state who is outside the state for a temporary or transitory purpose." (d): a domiciliary
-- absent for at least 546 consecutive days under an employment-related contract (returns of up to 45 days a year
-- disregarded) is outside the state for other than a temporary purpose -- unless intangible income exceeds $200,000 in a
-- year the contract is in effect. s 17016: more than nine months in the state raises a presumption of residence, which
-- "may be overcome by satisfactory evidence" of a temporary or transitory purpose.
GIVEN `in California for other than a temporary or transitory purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `domiciled in California and away only temporarily`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `away 546 days or more under an employment contract`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `intangible income over 200000`                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `months in California in the year`                           IS A NUMBER
      `the presumption is overcome`                                IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a resident` IF
        `in California for other than a temporary or transitory purpose`
    OR  (    `domiciled in California and away only temporarily`
         AND (    NOT (`away 546 days or more under an employment contract`)
              OR  `intangible income over 200000`))
    OR  (`months in California in the year` GREATER THAN 9 AND (NOT (`the presumption is overcome`)))

§§ `s 17073.5 -- the standard deduction (2025 figures)`

-- (a): $1,880 (single or separate) and $3,760 (head of household, surviving spouse, joint), recomputed each year by the FTB
-- under (d). For 2025 the FTB booklet gives $5,706 and $11,412 (annual-figures.json).
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2025 standard deduction` MEANS
    IF `status` EQUALS `single` OR `status` EQUALS `married or RDP filing separately`
    THEN 5706
    ELSE 11412

§§ `s 17041 -- the tax (2025 rate schedules)`

-- One row of a schedule: over `from`, the tax is `base` plus `rate` of the excess.
GIVEN `taxable income` IS A NUMBER, `from` IS A NUMBER, `base` IS A NUMBER, `rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the row` MEANS `base` PLUS (`rate` TIMES (`taxable income` MINUS `from`))

-- Schedule X: s 17041(a)(1), single and married filing separately.
GIVEN `ti` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`schedule X` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `ti` AT MOST 11079  THEN `the row` `ti` 0 0 (1%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 26264  THEN `the row` `ti` 11079 110.79 (2%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 41452  THEN `the row` `ti` 26264 414.49 (4%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 57542  THEN `the row` `ti` 41452 1022.01 (6%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 72724  THEN `the row` `ti` 57542 1987.41 (8%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 371479 THEN `the row` `ti` 72724 3201.97 (9.3%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 445771 THEN `the row` `ti` 371479 30986.19 (10.3%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 742953 THEN `the row` `ti` 445771 38638.27 (11.3%)
           OTHERWISE `the row` `ti` 742953 72219.84 (12.3%)

-- Schedule Y: s 17041(a)(2) and s 17045, joint returns and surviving spouses.
GIVEN `ti` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`schedule Y` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `ti` AT MOST 22158   THEN `the row` `ti` 0 0 (1%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 52528   THEN `the row` `ti` 22158 221.58 (2%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 82904   THEN `the row` `ti` 52528 828.98 (4%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 115084  THEN `the row` `ti` 82904 2044.02 (6%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 145448  THEN `the row` `ti` 115084 3974.82 (8%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 742958  THEN `the row` `ti` 145448 6403.94 (9.3%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 891542  THEN `the row` `ti` 742958 61972.37 (10.3%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 1485906 THEN `the row` `ti` 891542 77276.52 (11.3%)
           OTHERWISE `the row` `ti` 1485906 144439.65 (12.3%)

-- Schedule Z: s 17041(b), head of household.
GIVEN `ti` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`schedule Z` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `ti` AT MOST 22173   THEN `the row` `ti` 0 0 (1%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 52530   THEN `the row` `ti` 22173 221.73 (2%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 67716   THEN `the row` `ti` 52530 828.87 (4%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 83805   THEN `the row` `ti` 67716 1436.31 (6%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 98990   THEN `the row` `ti` 83805 2401.65 (8%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 505208  THEN `the row` `ti` 98990 3616.45 (9.3%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 606251  THEN `the row` `ti` 505208 41394.72 (10.3%)
           IF `ti` AT MOST 1010417 THEN `the row` `ti` 606251 51802.15 (11.3%)
           OTHERWISE `the row` `ti` 1010417 97472.91 (12.3%)

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 17041 tax` MEANS
    IF `a joint-type status` `status`
    THEN `schedule Y` `taxable income`
    ELSE IF `status` EQUALS `head of household`
         THEN `schedule Z` `taxable income`
         ELSE `schedule X` `taxable income`

-- s 17043(a): "an additional tax ... at the rate of 1 percent on that portion of a taxpayer's taxable income in excess of
-- one million dollars ($1,000,000)". (c): no credits against it, no filing-status doubling.
GIVEN `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 17043 additional tax` MEANS 1% TIMES max 0 (`taxable income` MINUS 1000000)

§§ `s 17054, s 17054.1 -- exemption credits (2025 figures)`

-- s 17054(a)-(d), recomputed by the FTB (2025: $153 personal, blind and senior; $475 each dependent). The personal credit
-- counts 1 (single, separate, head of household) or 2 (joint, surviving spouse); none for a person someone else can claim
-- as a dependent (the FTB form, line 6). Blind and senior credits count each spouse who qualifies.
DECLARE `Exemption facts` HAS
    `can be claimed as a dependent by someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
    `blind persons`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `persons 65 or older`                           IS A NUMBER
    `dependents`                                    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `e` IS AN `Exemption facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the personal, blind and senior credit count` MEANS
    (IF e's `can be claimed as a dependent by someone else`
     THEN 0
     ELSE IF `a joint-type status` `status` THEN 2 ELSE 1)
    PLUS e's `blind persons` PLUS e's `persons 65 or older`

-- s 17054.1: each credit "reduced by six dollars ($6) for each two thousand five hundred dollars ($2,500), or fraction
-- thereof, by which the taxpayer's federal adjusted gross income exceeds the threshold amount" ($1,250 for married filing
-- separately; $12 for the joint personal credit, which the count of 2 gives); thresholds recomputed annually (2025:
-- $252,203 single or separate; $504,411 joint or surviving spouse; $378,310 head of household). Never below zero.
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2025 phase-out threshold` MEANS
    IF `a joint-type status` `status`
    THEN 504411
    ELSE IF `status` EQUALS `head of household`
         THEN 378310
         ELSE 252203

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `federal AGI` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduction per credit` MEANS
    IF `federal AGI` AT MOST `the 2025 phase-out threshold` `status`
    THEN 0
    ELSE 6 TIMES `steps or fraction` (`federal AGI` MINUS `the 2025 phase-out threshold` `status`) (`the phase-out step` `status`)

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the phase-out step` MEANS
    IF `status` EQUALS `married or RDP filing separately`
    THEN 1250
    ELSE 2500

GIVEN `excess` IS A NUMBER, `step` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`steps or fraction` MEANS
    IF FLOOR (`excess` DIVIDED BY `step`) EQUALS (`excess` DIVIDED BY `step`)
    THEN `excess` DIVIDED BY `step`
    ELSE FLOOR (`excess` DIVIDED BY `step`) PLUS 1

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `federal AGI` IS A NUMBER, `e` IS AN `Exemption facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the exemption credits` MEANS
    (max 0 ((153 MINUS `the reduction per credit` `status` `federal AGI`) TIMES `the personal, blind and senior credit count` `status` `e`))
    PLUS (max 0 ((475 MINUS `the reduction per credit` `status` `federal AGI`) TIMES e's `dependents`))

§§ `s 17053.5 -- renter's credit (2025)`

-- (a)(1): for joint filers, heads of household and surviving spouses with AGI at or under the limit, $120 (taxable years
-- before 2026); for other individuals, $60. The AGI limits are recomputed annually (2025: $107,988 and $53,994). (a)(2): a
-- married couple filing separately share one credit; the equal division, $60 each, is used (finding 5). (c): a "qualified
-- renter" was a resident and rented and occupied a California principal residence for at least half the year; the (d)
-- exclusions are folded into that fact. Nonrefundable: a credit against "net tax".
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `California AGI` IS A NUMBER, `qualified renter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2025 renter's credit` MEANS
    IF NOT `qualified renter`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `status` EQUALS `single` OR `status` EQUALS `married or RDP filing separately`
         THEN IF `California AGI` AT MOST 53994 THEN 60 ELSE 0
         ELSE IF `California AGI` AT MOST 107988 THEN 120 ELSE 0

§§ `The tax for 2025`

DECLARE `Return` HAS
    `taxable year`                 IS A NUMBER
    `full-year resident`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `status`                       IS A `Filing status`
    `federal AGI`                  IS A NUMBER
    `California AGI`               IS A NUMBER
    `elects the standard deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `itemized deductions`          IS A NUMBER
    `exemption facts`              IS AN `Exemption facts`
    `qualified renter`             IS A BOOLEAN

-- Taxable income: California AGI less the standard deduction (or itemized deductions), never below nil. "Net tax"
-- (s 17039): the s 17041 tax less the exemption credits and the renter's credit, never below nil; then the s 17043 tax,
-- against which no credit is allowed.
GIVEN r IS A `Return`
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`the 2025 tax` MEANS
    IF NOT (r's `taxable year` EQUALS 2025)
    THEN `not covered` `this encoding has the Franchise Tax Board's figures for the 2025 taxable year only`
    ELSE IF NOT (r's `full-year resident`)
         THEN `not covered` `the tax of a part-year resident or nonresident is not encoded`
         ELSE `answered` ((max 0 (`regular tax` MINUS `credits`)) PLUS `the s 17043 additional tax` `taxable income`)
    WHERE
        `deduction` MEANS
            IF r's `elects the standard deduction`
            THEN `the 2025 standard deduction` (r's `status`)
            ELSE r's `itemized deductions`
        `taxable income` MEANS max 0 (r's `California AGI` MINUS `deduction`)
        `regular tax` MEANS `the s 17041 tax` (r's `status`) `taxable income`
        `credits` MEANS (`the exemption credits` (r's `status`) (r's `federal AGI`) (r's `exemption facts`)) PLUS (`the 2025 renter's credit` (r's `status`) (r's `California AGI`) (r's `qualified renter`))

§§ `Duties and elections`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `the taxpayer`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `elect the standard deduction`
    `include each dependent's identifying number or the information the Board prescribes`

-- s 17073.5(a): "A taxpayer may elect to take a standard deduction".
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the standard deduction election` `who` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MAY   `elect the standard deduction`

-- s 17054(d)(2)(A)(ii): no dependent credit "unless" the dependent's identifying number is on the return, or, for a
-- dependent ineligible for one, "the taxpayer shall provide information to identify the individual in the form and the
-- manner as prescribed by the Franchise Tax Board". (B): a disallowance may be assessed like a math error. No time.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to identify dependents` `who` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MUST  `include each dependent's identifying number or the information the Board prescribes`

-- =====================================================================================================================
§ `Questions for the taxpayer`

§§ `Am I a California resident?`

@export Am I a California resident for personal income tax (Rev. & Tax. Code ss 17014, 17016)?
GIVEN `I am in California for more than a temporary purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in California for other than a temporary or transitory purpose?
      `California is my domicile and I am away temporarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is California your domicile, and are you outside the state only for a temporary or transitory purpose?
      `I am away 546 days on a work contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you away for at least 546 consecutive days under an employment-related contract (ignoring up to 45 days of visits a year)?
      `my intangible income is over 200000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a year the contract is in effect, is your income from stocks, bonds and other intangibles over $200,000?
      `months I spent in California` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many months of the year did you spend in California?
      `I can show my stay was temporary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If over nine months: can you show by satisfactory evidence that you were in California only for a temporary or transitory purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I a California resident` MEANS
    `a resident` `I am in California for more than a temporary purpose` `California is my domicile and I am away temporarily` `I am away 546 days on a work contract` `my intangible income is over 200000` `months I spent in California` `I can show my stay was temporary`

§§ `How much is my 2025 tax?`

@export What are my 2025 California exemption credits after the high-income phase-out (Rev. & Tax. Code ss 17054, 17054.1)?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, married or RDP filing jointly, married or RDP filing separately, head of household, or qualifying surviving spouse or RDP
      `my federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `someone can claim me as a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can someone else claim you (or your spouse) as a dependent?
      `blind people` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you and your spouse/RDP are visually impaired?
      `people 65 or older` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you and your spouse/RDP were 65 or older by the end of 2025?
      `my dependents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents (not yourself or your spouse/RDP) do you claim?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What are my 2025 exemption credits` MEANS
    `the exemption credits` `my filing status` `my federal AGI` (`Exemption facts` WITH
        `can be claimed as a dependent by someone else` IS `someone can claim me as a dependent`
        `blind persons`                                 IS `blind people`
        `persons 65 or older`                           IS `people 65 or older`
        `dependents`                                    IS `my dependents`)

@export What is my 2025 California renter's credit (Rev. & Tax. Code s 17053.5)?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, married or RDP filing jointly, married or RDP filing separately, head of household, or qualifying surviving spouse or RDP
      `my California AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your California adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `I am a qualified renter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a California resident who rented and lived in a California home (not property-tax exempt, and not living with someone who claims you as a dependent) as your main home for at least half of 2025?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my 2025 renter's credit` MEANS
    `the 2025 renter's credit` `my filing status` `my California AGI` `I am a qualified renter`

@export How much California personal income tax do I owe for 2025 as a full-year resident, before the CalEITC, Young Child Tax Credit and other credits (Rev. & Tax. Code ss 17041, 17043, 17053.5, 17054, 17073.5)?
GIVEN `taxable year` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable year (only 2025 is covered)
      `I was a resident all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a California resident for the whole year?
      `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, married or RDP filing jointly, married or RDP filing separately, head of household, or qualifying surviving spouse or RDP
      `my federal AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `my California AGI` IS A NUMBER @desc Your California adjusted gross income (federal AGI with the California adjustments), in US dollars
      `I take the standard deduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you take the California standard deduction rather than itemise?
      `my itemized deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc Your California itemized deductions, if you itemise, in US dollars
      `someone can claim me as a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can someone else claim you (or your spouse) as a dependent?
      `blind people` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you and your spouse/RDP are visually impaired?
      `people 65 or older` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you and your spouse/RDP were 65 or older by the end of 2025?
      `my dependents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents do you claim?
      `I am a qualified renter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you rent and live in a California home as your main home for at least half of 2025 (see the renter's credit question)?
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`How much California income tax do I owe for 2025` MEANS
    `the 2025 tax` (`Return` WITH
        `taxable year`                  IS `taxable year`
        `full-year resident`            IS `I was a resident all year`
        `status`                        IS `my filing status`
        `federal AGI`                   IS `my federal AGI`
        `California AGI`                IS `my California AGI`
        `elects the standard deduction` IS `I take the standard deduction`
        `itemized deductions`           IS `my itemized deductions`
        `exemption facts`               IS (`Exemption facts` WITH
            `can be claimed as a dependent by someone else` IS `someone can claim me as a dependent`
            `blind persons`                                 IS `blind people`
            `persons 65 or older`                           IS `people 65 or older`
            `dependents`                                    IS `my dependents`)
        `qualified renter`              IS `I am a qualified renter`)
